        "original_id": "25a10486-eea2-5780-9afd-5be58c358e0e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Keri Hulme, Orson Scott Card, Bridgette Allen\n- Works: The Bone People, Ender's Game, Speaker for the Dead, Hooks and Feelers\n- Awards: Booker Prize, Hugo Awards, Nebula Awards\n\nFacts:\n- In 1985, Keri Hulme's only novel, \"The Bone People,\" won the Booker Prize.\n- In 1985, Orson Scott Card's novel \"Ender's Game\" won both the Hugo Award and the Nebula Award.\n- In 1986, Orson Scott Card's sequel \"Speaker for the Dead\" won both the Hugo Award and the Nebula Award.\n- Orson Scott Card became the only author to win both science fiction's top U.S. prizes in consecutive years.\n- Bridgette Allen starred in the film \"Hooks and Feelers,\" which was adapted from a story by Keri Hulme.",
